<section class="cb-section cb-about-story">
  <div class="cb-story">
    <div class="cb-story__photo" style="background-image:url('catalog/view/image/craftboat/collection-story.png')"></div>
    <div class="cb-story__copy">
      <p class="cb-kicker">About us</p>
      <h2 class="cb-display">A studio tied to the craft of Jaipur.</h2>
      <p>Based in Jaipur, India, our roots are tied to the multitude of art and design this city harbours. Working extensively with recycled paper and natural-fibre textile, we connect these endeavours with traditional Indian craftsmanship.</p>
      <p>The collections reflect an <strong>intentional use of material and craft</strong>, and an honouring of slower processes. We have always aimed to make long-lasting, functional products. Today, led by the same beliefs, Craft Boat has grown into a <strong>multidisciplinary design and manufacturing studio</strong>.</p>
      <p>Partnering with businesses that encourage artisan-made products, we hope to make space for <strong>kinder choices</strong> to exist and flourish — a sense of harmony and flexibility that radiates well beyond our studio walls.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="cb-cream cb-about-values">
  <div class="cb-head">
    <div>
      <p class="cb-kicker">What we value</p>
      <h2>Four pillars, held in the work.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>Here are the core pillars that reflect what we truly value.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="cb-about__pillars">
    <article id="craft">
      <p class="cb-num">01</p>
      <h3>Craft &amp; community</h3>
      <p>At the heart of Craft Boat there is a fundamental <strong>understanding of the core behaviour</strong> of Indian craft techniques, and of the interactions between people, ideas, craft and material.</p>
      <p>Our community is what holds us afloat — our boat. We try to make choices that <strong>nurture connections</strong> and <strong>foster a community</strong> of like-minded people who come together to celebrate crafts and makers from across India.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="circularity">
      <p class="cb-num">02</p>
      <h3>Circularity</h3>
      <p>In the studio there is always an <strong>organic discussion</strong> about how to reuse materials and reduce waste when designing any product. New craft techniques have let us <strong>close the loop</strong> and reimagine waste through a <em>shift of form</em>.</p>
      <p><a href="{{ paper }}">Read more about how we close the loop →</a></p>
    </article>
    <article id="analog">
      <p class="cb-num">03</p>
      <h3>Analog</h3>
      <p>Over the years we have tried to design <strong>timeless pieces</strong> which radiate thoughtfulness. Following the traditions of product utility and primitive design techniques, we want the generations after us to <strong>use and cherish</strong> the objects we make.</p>
    </article>
    <article id="flow">
      <p class="cb-num">04</p>
      <h3>Flow</h3>
      <p><strong>Continuously experimenting</strong> with form and function, open to new craft techniques, and always <strong>connecting the dots</strong> with like-minded brands — this is how we have stayed <strong>fluid</strong> in our design process.</p>
      <p><a href="{{ collaborations }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read more about our collaborations →</a></p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

